{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     navbar/auth — Ghost Members, in the bar.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     data-portal is Ghost's own hook: its Portal script binds these and opens
     the right screen. No JavaScript of ours, and the href is a real fragment
     so it still routes with Portal blocked.

     ── SIGN IN IS AN ICON, SUBSCRIBE IS THE BUTTON ──────────────────────────
     .ns-navicon is NSDS's borderless bar control — the same thing the theme
     switch sits in — and it carries a TRANSPARENT 1px border rather than
     none, so the box does not resize when the border appears on hover.

     Subscribe stays a filled button, and that is design principle 3 rather
     than an oversight: brand blue is the only colour that means "interactive",
     so a bar with two bordered buttons in it has two obvious next actions and
     therefore none. On this site the newsletter IS the action.

     An icon-only control needs a real accessible name, so aria-label carries
     what the removed text used to say.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
    <div class="ns-topnav__auth">
        {{#unless @member}}
            <a class="ns-navicon" href="#/portal/signin" data-portal="signin"
               aria-label="{{t "Sign in"}}">{{> "icons/user-circle"}}</a>
            <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary ns-btn--sm" href="#/portal/signup" data-portal="signup">
                {{> "icons/envelope"}} {{t "Subscribe"}}
            </a>
        {{else}}
            <a class="ns-navicon" href="#/portal/account" data-portal="account"
               aria-label="{{t "Your account"}}">{{> "icons/user-circle"}}</a>
        {{/unless}}
    </div>
{{/if}}
